  "briefing": {
    "title": "THE RUINS",
    "story": [
      "Halex is dead and the Directorate on Aether Prime is a headless thing — but it",
      "has not stopped moving. Its last flights are digging in on the glass-flats above",
      "the Vein, and the ground under them has not finished answering the Warden.",
      "",
      "SERA VANE: \"Three spore towers. The planet grew them itself, long before us — every",
      "thread of what you did at the Vein runs through them. Whoever holds the towers",
      "holds the wound. Right now the Directorate does.\"",
      "",
      "MARSHAL CORR: \"One more campaign, Warden. Then we find out what we bought.\""
    ],
    "objectives": [
      "Take and hold the three spore towers (45s each)",
      "Keep the Construction Yard standing until the towers are anchored",
      "Vane must survive (O selects, F1/F2 cast)"
    ]
  },
  "debrief": {
    "win": [
      "The towers hum in a chord the planet chose. The fracture lines slow, then stop.",
      "The continent holds — for now — and the Directorate survivors pull back toward",
      "the last uplink batteries on the far flats.",
      "CORR: \"Anchored. Whatever you decided at the Vein, it just held.\""
    ],
    "lose": [
      "The towers fall silent one by one. The crust opens along the fracture lines,",
      "and Aether Prime — sealed or bound, it no longer matters — becomes a tomb."
    ]
  },
